# AGENTS.md

## Overview
Brief 1-2 sentence description of the repository, key framework components, and primary purpose.

## Architecture & Layout
High-level architectural pointers. For full layout details, see [architecture.md](architecture.md).
- `src/` — Primary application source code
- `tests/` — Automated test suite
- `docs/` — Architecture Decision Records and specifications

## Core Commands
Essential commands for building, testing, and developing:
- Build: `npm run build` or `cargo build`
- Test: `pytest` or `npm test`
- Dev: `npm run dev`

## Non-Negotiable Rules / Invariants
1. **Test-Driven Work**: MUST have a failing test before writing production code. (details: [.agent/rules/test-driven-development.md](.agent/rules/test-driven-development.md))
2. **Coding Conventions**: MUST follow naming standards and file headers. (details: [.agent/rules/coding-conventions.md](.agent/rules/coding-conventions.md))
3. **No Direct Commits**: NEVER commit directly to main; ALWAYS use isolated feature branches. (details: [.agent/rules/git-operations.md](.agent/rules/git-operations.md))

## On-Demand Skills & Reference Index
- Read [.agent/rules/](.agent/rules/) when working in specific architectural layers.
- Read [docs/architecture/](docs/architecture/) when reviewing system designs or known pitfalls.
